 "last_rtl_message": {
  "stage": "rtl-design-creation",
  "visit": 4,
  "text": "DONE. The synthesis failure came from `rtl/jtag_waive.vlt` being listed in `build.yaml` sources, which made Vivado try to read it as Verilog. I have not re-run the Vivado build, `check` or `simulate`. Lint now passes.\n\n- **`build.yaml`:** I removed the `.vlt` line from the sources. `jtag_bus.sv` is still in the sources and is untouched.\n- **`rtl/a_lint_waive.sv`:** This file was empty, so I moved the Verilator waiver for the unused `tdo` and `cmd_s[45]` in `jtag_bus.sv` into it. The waiver sits inside `ifdef VERILATOR`, so Vivado and Icarus never see it.\n- **Lint workaround:** The waiver only took effect once I added `-match \"*\"` to the `lint_off` line. I don't know why the plain `-file` form was ignored.\n- **`rtl/jtag_waive.vlt`:** The file is still on disk, but nothing builds from it now. I can't delete files here."
 },
